Write the HTML body of a podcast episode description, with the text aligned {{ direction }}.

Structure, in order:
1. An `<h3>` holding a single title that summarises all the article titles below, translated to
   {{ language }}. Where several titles concern the same company, fold them together.
2. Two `<br>` tags.
3. One link per article, each on its own line separated by `<br>`. Each link takes its text from
   the matching entry in article_links_titles.
{% if episode_content_link %}
4. Two `<br>` tags.
5. A link to the episode content. Its link text is "link to the episode content", translated to
   {{ language }}.
{% endif %}

Rules:
- Keep article_links and article_links_titles in the same order; link N uses title N.
- Return an HTML fragment only — no `<html>`, `<head>` or `<body>` wrapper, no markdown fences.
- No preamble such as "here is the summary", and no commentary of any kind.

article_links={{ links }}
article_links_titles={{ titles }}
{% if episode_content_link %}
episode_content_link={{ episode_content_link }}
{% endif %}
